meta {
  name: email-links
  seq: 25
}

docs {
  Manual test of the verify and cancel links. Every request here skips itself unless bruno/.env contains RUN_EMAIL_LINKS=true, so a normal collection run never touches them: the tokens only exist in the backend console until the emails do, and they work for one test only.

  To run them, one at a time and in order:
  1. Add RUN_EMAIL_LINKS=true to bruno/.env.
  2. Send "Login - admin" for adminToken, then "Create reservation - form", and copy the token at the end of the printed verify link into bruno/.env as VERIFY_TOKEN (it lasts 30 minutes).
  3. Send requests 1 and 2. Request 2 prints the cancel link: copy its token into bruno/.env as CANCEL_TOKEN.
  4. Send the remaining requests.
  5. Remove RUN_EMAIL_LINKS from bruno/.env, or the next full run will fail on the used tokens.

  Request 1 sets maxOnlineTables to 0 and back to 36 inside one single request: there is no separate setup request that could run alone.
}
